   "observation": "The leg poses do not describe a run. Contact (F000/F010) is an over-striding, straight-legged heel dig with the thigh at -35; the hip then hyper-extends to +40 (F010 left leg, the thigh is far behind the body with the knee still bent 30), and the recovery whips from +40 to -55 in 5 frames with the knee jumping 30 to 95 in 3 frames (accel spikes of 14-19 deg/frame^2 on LowerLeg at frames 1-3 and 10-13, velocity corners at 3, 5, 10, 13, 15). The planted foot also skates: its speed goes 0.15, 0.37, 0.43, 0.37, 0.32, 0.27 studs/frame (std 0.09) because the thigh eases out of the contact. Fix: land closer under the body (thigh -22, knee 14), absorb to a 42 deg knee at frame 3, push off to +22 at frame 7, start folding the trailing knee in flight (70 at the opposite contact) into a 105 deg recovery, and space the stance thigh keys so the foot travels at a steady 0.2 studs/frame.",
